WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.160
A 72 gpu rubin rack now carries 20.7 terabytes of hbm4 for inference. This is AI Chips &amp; Data Centers, episode 42. After the rack, Korea's memory meetings, a foundry rethink with TSMC, and a tear-down of why an old gpu can still earn rent. Serve the home-walk the AS-Rock rack booth at the OCP Summit in San Jose and found the XGM rack, a 48-rack unit MGX design with a 5,000-amp bus bar,

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:36.260
R, and a liquid manifold. 18 Vera Ruben compute trays and 9 NV-Link 6 switch trays hold 36

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:46.160
Vera CPUs. Nvidia lists the rack at 3,600 petaflops of sparse NVFP4 inference and 2,520 petaflops

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:54.160
of dense NVFP4 training. Each Ruben GPU is listed at 288 gigabytes of HBM4. Four shelves,

00:00:54.160 --> 00:01:02.480
each rated at 110 kW, use 618.3 kW supplies and bulk capacitors, with cooling distribution in

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:08.300
the rack, in the row, on a rear door, or in a liquid to air sidecar. Every compute tray is liquid

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:15.340
cooled, with 8800 gigabit ports off ConnectX 9 Supernix, and 2400 gigabit ports off a blue field

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:23.427
for DPU. Intel measured a Xeon 6 instance at 1.66 times the agent task throughput of a fifth generation

00:01:23.427 --> 00:01:30.707
an AMD EPYC instance, and 4.5 times an ARM V9.2A instance, on a healthcare terminal

00:01:30.707 --> 00:01:31.387
bench trace.

00:01:31.947 --> 00:01:37.627
The run held 24-way concurrency for 60 minutes, with the same code inputs and agent paths

00:01:37.627 --> 00:01:38.727
on every platform.

00:01:39.387 --> 00:01:44.407
Intel recorded the workflow and replayed that trace, so the gap is the machine, not a different

00:01:44.407 --> 00:01:45.187
choice of tools.

00:01:45.727 --> 00:01:50.947
The healthcare set covered clinical notes, evidence search, fraud checks, and lab diagnostics

00:01:50.947 --> 00:01:51.927
among other jobs.

00:01:51.927 --> 00:01:55.047
Nithya Rao and Sao Miyabulia wrote the piece.

00:01:55.986 --> 00:02:01.506
Martin Lin, marketing director at McCronix, told E.E. Times Taiwan that AI is rewriting

00:02:01.506 --> 00:02:04.166
memory architecture, not just adding demand.

00:02:04.746 --> 00:02:11.446
McCronix lifted 2026 capital spending to $37.8 billion new Taiwan dollars to grow 12-inch

00:02:11.446 --> 00:02:16.086
wafer output for 3D, NOR, NAND, EMMC, and related parts.

00:02:16.726 --> 00:02:22.146
Lin set an older rack carried about 600-800 NOR flash devices, and the newest rack

00:02:22.146 --> 00:02:27.846
carries more than a thousand for boot, firmware, control, and security as controllers and switches

00:02:27.846 --> 00:02:34.826
multiply. Market data in that article put the memory market above $20 billion in 2025 and near

00:02:34.826 --> 00:02:43.406
$70 billion in 2026, with NOOR, SLC, NAND, and low capacity EMMC together around $24 billion this year.

00:02:44.046 --> 00:02:50.646
The same piece treats high bandwidth flash, built on 3D and A&amp;D as a fatter tier for data that does

00:02:50.646 --> 00:02:56.226
not have to live in HBM, and says install, qualification, and yield ramp can take two to

00:02:56.226 --> 00:02:56.806
three years.

00:02:58.146 --> 00:03:04.126
WCCF tech says Elon Musk laid out Colossus 2 as announced plans, not an energized site.

00:03:04.666 --> 00:03:10.606
Hall is called macro harder, mini hard, and gun range, each with roughly 220,000 blackwell

00:03:10.606 --> 00:03:11.426
GPUs.

00:03:11.926 --> 00:03:18.366
Semi-analysis says the 2027 US data center build is largely locked in, while a long Texas

00:03:18.366 --> 00:03:23.726
permit freeze is now the single biggest risk to 2028, and both parties are campaigning

00:03:23.726 --> 00:03:24.566
on tighter rules.

00:03:25.949 --> 00:03:31.729
ETCIO, drawing on the Korea Herald, says Sam Altman sat with about 50 Samsung executives

00:03:31.729 --> 00:03:37.869
in Yongin on Saturday, then with SK Chairman Choi Tae-won and executives from SK Heinex

00:03:37.869 --> 00:03:42.349
and SK Telecom, and that no new supply or investment deal was announced.

00:03:42.829 --> 00:03:48.089
In that account, Altman said merely adopting AI will no longer lock in a lasting edge.

00:03:48.089 --> 00:03:56.509
Trend4 sees HBM's blended-average selling price possibly up 121% in 2027, from 2026.

00:03:57.269 --> 00:04:00.489
Samsung said its HBM for 2027 is sold out.

00:04:01.069 --> 00:04:08.329
SK HighNix said output through 2029 is effectively spoken for, in firm contracts and volumes still under negotiation,

00:04:08.909 --> 00:04:13.649
and sales head Kim Kite said customers want more than twice what the company can ship.

00:04:13.649 --> 00:04:20.309
The Harold says open AI has reportedly lined up about $11 billion against an opening $30 billion

00:04:20.309 --> 00:04:27.049
target. Numbers nobody has independently confirmed, and that the October 2025 Stargate sketch of

00:04:27.049 --> 00:04:33.409
900,000 DRAM wafer starts a month was a production target, not a binding order. International

00:04:33.409 --> 00:04:39.309
business times, citing the Wall Street Journal, adds that a hoped-for valuation slipped from about

00:04:39.309 --> 00:04:45.589
$1.4 trillion to about $1.25 trillion, and that the raise was later trimmed to a target

00:04:45.589 --> 00:04:46.929
of as much as $20 billion.

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:54.660
After casting TSMC as a subcontractor at best, Musk is now reported by Digitimes through

00:04:54.660 --> 00:05:01.640
WCCF Tech to be reopening terms with operational control, joint investment, and advance packaging

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:02.380
on the table.

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:09.080
TSMC Chief CC Way said on the latest earnings call that talks with Musk are underway, and

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:12.220
and that TSMC would have to run the plans for a deal to work.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:17.560
The TerraFab idea in that report aims at more than a terawatt of computing capacity.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:20.600
It is a report of talks, not a signed contract.

00:05:21.683 --> 00:05:29.063
Biggo Finance puts TSMC's cumulative Arizona investment at $265 billion, including an extra

00:05:29.063 --> 00:05:34.423
100 billion announced this year, and calls that the largest foreign investment on the U.S. record.

00:05:34.423 --> 00:05:41.903
100. The first fab is operational. TSMC employs about 3,500 people in Arizona and plans to

00:05:41.903 --> 00:05:47.783
hire 2,500 more. Collier's numbers in the piece show industrial vacancy on Phoenix's

00:05:47.783 --> 00:05:54.543
northwestern edge falling from 16% a year earlier to 8% in June. Zillow figures there put

00:05:54.543 --> 00:06:00.903
six-year home price gains in North Gateway and Desert View at about 53% against 42% for

00:06:00.903 --> 00:06:06.583
the city, and after TSMC took about 900 acres in North Park, the planned housing there

00:06:06.583 --> 00:06:12.363
was cut by about 20%. Yahoo Finance reports that ACE Nano-CAM has developed three new

00:06:12.363 --> 00:06:18.088
semiconductor materials for power devices and advanced packaging. A token is the barrel,

00:06:18.388 --> 00:06:25.008
and each GPU generation is a well. EE times uses a Gartner forecast and an A16Z rent chart

00:06:25.008 --> 00:06:30.028
to say the cost of that barrel is mostly energy, plus whether the chip can do the job at all.

00:06:30.028 --> 00:06:34.168
Newer Silicon that finishes more work per watt is the easy well.

00:06:34.628 --> 00:06:36.728
It stays open when the token price falls.

00:06:37.348 --> 00:06:38.628
The hardwell is shut first.

00:06:39.308 --> 00:06:41.828
Rant above a depreciation line is not profit.

00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:47.248
Power, cooling, networking, the building, and the cost of borrowing still come out.

00:06:47.828 --> 00:06:53.828
Gartner, as EE Times reports it, has providers spending close to $1 trillion on AI infrastructure

00:06:53.828 --> 00:06:58.848
in 2026, and another $6 trillion from 2027 through 2030.

00:06:58.848 --> 00:07:04.748
To pay for that, cover borrowing and still earn a 12% return, those data center owners

00:07:04.748 --> 00:07:08.528
would need about $8.5 trillion of revenue through 2030.

00:07:09.188 --> 00:07:13.888
Gartner expects at most $3.6 trillion of AI revenue to reach those halls.

00:07:14.528 --> 00:07:19.728
The gap is more than $3.5 trillion of spending that could face write downs by 2030.

00:07:20.508 --> 00:07:25.568
EE times flags that as a risk estimate under Gartner's assumptions, not a forecast that

00:07:25.568 --> 00:07:27.068
the whole sum will be written off.

00:07:27.068 --> 00:07:32.948
On the same math, more than 80% of Neoclouds would no longer stand as independent companies.

00:07:33.588 --> 00:07:38.408
Epoch AI, cited in the piece, estimates the price of a given benchmark score has fallen

00:07:38.408 --> 00:07:40.968
about 13 times a year since 2023.

00:07:41.708 --> 00:07:45.488
On the tests, it tracks, cheaper tokens can invite new jobs.

00:07:46.028 --> 00:07:49.688
Nothing in the chart promises that use grows faster than the price falls.

00:07:50.208 --> 00:07:55.508
If use only doubles while a scored result gets 13 times cheaper, revenue still shrinks.

00:07:55.508 --> 00:08:02.588
A 16z on Orn rents as of October 19, drew each Nvidia generation from its first observed

00:08:02.588 --> 00:08:07.328
rent down to 0 over 6 years, about the right off window hyperscalers use.

00:08:07.928 --> 00:08:10.088
Every generation was renting above that line.

00:08:10.648 --> 00:08:13.748
The H-200 sat 143% above it.

00:08:14.248 --> 00:08:19.328
Most of that gap opened after April when token demand took off, and for most of their lives

00:08:19.328 --> 00:08:21.168
these chips had rented below the line.

00:08:21.688 --> 00:08:24.688
A busy well can still lose money once the power bill is paid.

00:08:24.688 --> 00:08:28.868
Interactive and agent work wants low latency and the newest memory.

00:08:29.468 --> 00:08:34.448
Overnight documents, synthetic data and evaluations mostly want a cheap token and barely

00:08:34.448 --> 00:08:35.148
notice delay.

00:08:35.708 --> 00:08:40.368
A chip whose capital is already written off with power, cooling, and upkeep left as the

00:08:40.368 --> 00:08:43.688
main costs can be the cheapest barrel for that second market.

00:08:44.268 --> 00:08:45.748
There is not one token price.

00:08:46.328 --> 00:08:50.988
Keeping every generation online stops being the right call when a newer generation is arriving

00:08:50.988 --> 00:08:56.028
in volume, and the token price has fallen far enough that an unpaid-off older chip's energy

00:08:56.028 --> 00:09:01.022
cost exceeds what even the latency-blind jobs will pay. On the horizon,

00:09:01.362 --> 00:09:07.962
McCronix expects North Flash, SLC-NAND, and EMMC prices to rise further in the third and fourth

00:09:07.962 --> 00:09:15.302
quarters of 2026, then sit at those higher levels. Two more TSMC Arizona fabs are expected to be finished

00:09:15.302 --> 00:09:20.982
by 2030. Microsoft plans to scale its Maya accelerators to multi-gigawatt deployments

00:09:20.982 --> 00:09:27.382
from 2027, claiming 40% more tokens per megawatt, a figure E.E. time says has not been

00:09:27.382 --> 00:09:28.462
independently checked.

00:09:29.323 --> 00:09:34.683
Before we go, watch whether those sole meetings turn the 900,000 wafer Stargate sketch into

00:09:34.683 --> 00:09:36.103
a funded supply contract.

